{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"agent_message","text":"\n\nAll tests pass. Here's a summary of the SQLAlchemy 2.x modernization:\n\n**Changes Made:**\n\n- **`app/repository.py`**: Converted from legacy `session.query()` to SQLAlchemy 2.x `select()` statements. Removed auto-commit from `create_entry()` so callers manage transaction boundaries.\n\n- **`app/worker.py`**: Uses `session_factory.begin()` context manager for explicit transaction boundaries. When `settle_entry` or `settle_batch` raise an exception, the transaction automatically rolls back, preserving the original status.\n\n- **`app/admin_cli.py`**: Uses `session_factory.begin()` for transaction management. `dry_run=True` mode no longer modifies the entry status, so no rollback is needed - the status simply isn't changed.\n\n- **`docs/deploy/sqlalchemy2-cutover.md`**: Updated documentation reflecting the new SQLAlchemy 2.x semantics and transaction boundary patterns."}}
